{"name":"Blue Lagoon","hex":"#00626f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blue Lagoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cocktail made with blue curaçao."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blue_Lagoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Blue Lagoon (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Lagoon is a coming-of-age romance novel written by Henry De Vere Stacpoole, first published by T. Fisher Unwin in 1908. The Blue Lagoon explores themes of love, childhood innocence, and conflict between civilisation and nature."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/The_Blue_Lagoon_Stacpoole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blue_Lagoon_(novel)","wikidata":"Q3822730"},{"title":"The Blue Lagoon (1923 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Lagoon is a lost 1923 British-South African silent film adaptation of Henry De Vere Stacpoole's 1908 novel of the same name about children who come of age while stranded on a tropical island. It is the first screen adaptation of the story, and two additional adaptations appeared in 1949 and 1980, with both versions achieving commercial success."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_2.jpg/330px-The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blue_Lagoon_(1923_film)","wikidata":"Q3986025"},{"title":"Blue Lagoon (geothermal spa)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Lagoon is a geothermal spa in southwestern Iceland. The spa is located in a lava field 5 km (3.1 mi) from Grindavík and in front of Mount Þorbjörn on the Reykjanes Peninsula, in a location favourable for geothermal power, and is supplied by water used in the nearby Svartsengi geothermal power station. The Blue Lagoon is approximately 20 km (12 mi) from Keflavík International Airport, and is one of the most visited tourist attractions in Iceland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/00/Blue_Lagoon_Main_Building.JPG/330px-Blue_Lagoon_Main_Building.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Lagoon_(geothermal_spa)","wikidata":"Q886946"},{"title":"Lagoon","blocks":[{"text":"A lagoon is a shallow body of water separated from a larger body of water by a narrow landform, such as a reef, a barrier island or islands, a barrier peninsula, or an isthmus. Lagoons are commonly divided into coastal lagoons and atoll lagoons. They have also been identified as occurring on mixed-sand and gravel coastlines. There is an overlap between bodies of water classified as coastal lagoons and bodies of water classified as estuaries. Lagoons are common coastal features around many parts of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/BalosLagoonCreta.jpg/330px-BalosLagoonCreta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagoon","wikidata":"Q187223"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_1.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_1.jpg/500px-The_Blue_Lagoon_%281923%29_-_still_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Doreen Wonfer, Arthur Pusey and Dick Cruickshanks in a shot from the film.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Blue_Lagoon_(1923)_-_still_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/BlueLagoon_Noface.jpg/500px-BlueLagoon_Noface.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wi